 "rules": {
  "accept": "no held bundle: take any bundle that verifies and has not expired. Held bundle: a lower version is bundle_rolled_back; the same version with another payload is bundle_forked, with the same payload it is unchanged (nothing new, not a refusal); version+1 whose prev_sha is not the held payload's is bundle_chain_broken; a higher version than version+1 is bundle_gap; another scope is bundle_chain_broken; past expires_at is bundle_expired.",
  "catch_up": "a client that missed versions takes the bundles since its held one, oldest first, all or nothing: every link verifies and chains, only the newest must be unexpired, and every link is verified with the keys valid at 'now', so a chain that spans a policy key rotation is refused and the client is re-bootstrapped.",
  "names": "bundle_rolled_back, bundle_forked, bundle_chain_broken, bundle_gap, bundle_expired",
  "prev_sha": "prev_sha is 'sha256:' plus the hex sha256 of the previous bundle's signed payload bytes; version 1 has an empty prev_sha; the chain is per tenant and scope."
 },
